    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.ai\n\n### Question\n\nHello there 👋🏾 \r\nLove love LOVE the suite of plugins! mini ai enables `ciq` which is just killer.\r\n\r\nI noticed that mini ai interferes with v0.12's `an` and `in` motions. These allow you to grow and shrink the node selection in visual mode.\r\n\r\nI tried disabling mini ai in visual mode per the docs but it seems to still trigger.\r\n\r\nThis is what I used to disable:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nlocal f_en = function(args) vim.b[args.buf].minianimate_disable = false end\r\nlocal enable_opts = { pattern = '[vV\\x16]*:*', callback = f_en }\r\nvim.api.nvim_create_autocmd('ModeChanged', enable_opts)\r\n\r\nlocal f_dis = function(args) vim.b[args.buf].minianimate_disable = true end\r\nlocal disable_opts = { pattern = '*:[vV\\x16]*', callback = f_dis }\r\nvim.api.nvim_create_autocmd('ModeChanged', disable_opts)\r\n```\r\n\r\nWhat could I try to keep the other parts of the config on? _I really_ dig `q` as an alias for `'` and `\"`\r\n\r\nThanks 🙏🏾 ",
    "bodyHTML": "<h3 dir=\"auto\">Contributing guidelines</h3>\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"> I have read <a href=\"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\">CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Module(s)</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">mini.ai</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Question</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Hello there 👋🏾<br>\nLove love LOVE the suite of plugins! mini ai enables <code class=\"notranslate\">ciq</code> which is just killer.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I noticed that mini ai interferes with v0.12's <code class=\"notranslate\">an</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">in</code> motions. These allow you to grow and shrink the node selection in visual mode.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I tried disabling mini ai in visual mode per the docs but it seems to still trigger.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This is what I used to disable:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-lua notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"local f_en = function(args) vim.b[args.buf].minianimate_disable = false end\nlocal enable_opts = { pattern = '[vV\\x16]*:*', callback = f_en }\nvim.api.nvim_create_autocmd('ModeChanged', enable_opts)\n\nlocal f_dis = function(args) vim.b[args.buf].minianimate_disable = true end\nlocal disable_opts = { pattern = '*:[vV\\x16]*', callback = f_dis }\nvim.api.nvim_create_autocmd('ModeChanged', disable_opts)\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-k\">local</span> <span class=\"pl-en\">f_en</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">function</span>(<span class=\"pl-smi\">args</span>) <span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">b</span>[<span class=\"pl-smi\">args</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">buf</span>].<span class=\"pl-e\">minianimate_disable</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">false</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">end</span>\n<span class=\"pl-k\">local</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">enable_opts</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> { <span class=\"pl-smi\">pattern</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>[vV<span class=\"pl-cce\">\\x16</span>]*:*<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-smi\">callback</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">f_en</span> }\n<span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">api</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">nvim_create_autocmd</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>ModeChanged<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-smi\">enable_opts</span>)\n\n<span class=\"pl-k\">local</span> <span class=\"pl-en\">f_dis</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">function</span>(<span class=\"pl-smi\">args</span>) <span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">b</span>[<span class=\"pl-smi\">args</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">buf</span>].<span class=\"pl-e\">minianimate_disable</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">true</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">end</span>\n<span class=\"pl-k\">local</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">disable_opts</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> { <span class=\"pl-smi\">pattern</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>*:[vV<span class=\"pl-cce\">\\x16</span>]*<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-smi\">callback</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">f_dis</span> }\n<span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">api</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">nvim_create_autocmd</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>ModeChanged<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-smi\">disable_opts</span>)</pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">What could I try to keep the other parts of the config on? <em>I really</em> dig <code class=\"notranslate\">q</code> as an alias for <code class=\"notranslate\">'</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">\"</code></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Thanks 🙏🏾</p>",
    "bodyText": "Contributing guidelines\n\n I have read CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\n\nModule(s)\nmini.ai\nQuestion\nHello there 👋🏾\nLove love LOVE the suite of plugins! mini ai enables ciq which is just killer.\nI noticed that mini ai interferes with v0.12's an and in motions. These allow you to grow and shrink the node selection in visual mode.\nI tried disabling mini ai in visual mode per the docs but it seems to still trigger.\nThis is what I used to disable:\nlocal f_en = function(args) vim.b[args.buf].minianimate_disable = false end\nlocal enable_opts = { pattern = '[vV\\x16]*:*', callback = f_en }\nvim.api.nvim_create_autocmd('ModeChanged', enable_opts)\n\nlocal f_dis = function(args) vim.b[args.buf].minianimate_disable = true end\nlocal disable_opts = { pattern = '*:[vV\\x16]*', callback = f_dis }\nvim.api.nvim_create_autocmd('ModeChanged', disable_opts)\nWhat could I try to keep the other parts of the config on? I really dig q as an alias for ' and \"\nThanks 🙏🏾",
