            "authorAssociation": "NONE",
            "body": "The buffer variable name is the issue in your snippet.\n\n`mini.ai` checks `vim.g.miniai_disable` and `vim.b.miniai_disable`. Your autocmd is setting `minianimate_disable`, which belongs to a different module name and will not disable `mini.ai`.\n\nFor a buffer-local Visual-mode toggle, the variable needs to be `miniai_disable` and it needs to be `true` while you want `mini.ai` disabled, for example:\n\n```lua\nvim.api.nvim_create_autocmd('ModeChanged', {\n  pattern = '*:[vV\\x16]*',\n  callback = function(args)\n    vim.b[args.buf].miniai_disable = true\n  end,\n})\n\nvim.api.nvim_create_autocmd('ModeChanged', {\n  pattern = '[vV\\x16]*:*',\n  callback = function(args)\n    vim.b[args.buf].miniai_disable = false\n  end,\n})\n```\n\nThat disables the whole `mini.ai` module for that buffer while the flag is set. If you only want to free Neovim's built-in `an`/`in` while keeping some `mini.ai` textobjects, the cleaner path is to adjust the `mini.ai` mappings rather than toggling `mini.ai` by mode.",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">The buffer variable name is the issue in your snippet.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><code class=\"notranslate\">mini.ai</code> checks <code class=\"notranslate\">vim.g.miniai_disable</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">vim.b.miniai_disable</code>. Your autocmd is setting <code class=\"notranslate\">minianimate_disable</code>, which belongs to a different module name and will not disable <code class=\"notranslate\">mini.ai</code>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">For a buffer-local Visual-mode toggle, the variable needs to be <code class=\"notranslate\">miniai_disable</code> and it needs to be <code class=\"notranslate\">true</code> while you want <code class=\"notranslate\">mini.ai</code> disabled, for example:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-lua notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"vim.api.nvim_create_autocmd('ModeChanged', {\n  pattern = '*:[vV\\x16]*',\n  callback = function(args)\n    vim.b[args.buf].miniai_disable = true\n  end,\n})\n\nvim.api.nvim_create_autocmd('ModeChanged', {\n  pattern = '[vV\\x16]*:*',\n  callback = function(args)\n    vim.b[args.buf].miniai_disable = false\n  end,\n})\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">api</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">nvim_create_autocmd</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>ModeChanged<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>, {\n  <span class=\"pl-smi\">pattern</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>*:[vV<span class=\"pl-cce\">\\x16</span>]*<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>,\n  <span class=\"pl-en\">callback</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">function</span>(<span class=\"pl-smi\">args</span>)\n    <span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">b</span>[<span class=\"pl-smi\">args</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">buf</span>].<span class=\"pl-e\">miniai_disable</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">true</span>\n  <span class=\"pl-k\">end</span>,\n})\n\n<span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">api</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">nvim_create_autocmd</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>ModeChanged<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>, {\n  <span class=\"pl-smi\">pattern</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>[vV<span class=\"pl-cce\">\\x16</span>]*:*<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>,\n  <span class=\"pl-en\">callback</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">function</span>(<span class=\"pl-smi\">args</span>)\n    <span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">b</span>[<span class=\"pl-smi\">args</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">buf</span>].<span class=\"pl-e\">miniai_disable</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">false</span>\n  <span class=\"pl-k\">end</span>,\n})</pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">That disables the whole <code class=\"notranslate\">mini.ai</code> module for that buffer while the flag is set. If you only want to free Neovim's built-in <code class=\"notranslate\">an</code>/<code class=\"notranslate\">in</code> while keeping some <code class=\"notranslate\">mini.ai</code> textobjects, the cleaner path is to adjust the <code class=\"notranslate\">mini.ai</code> mappings rather than toggling <code class=\"notranslate\">mini.ai</code> by mode.</p>",
            "bodyText": "The buffer variable name is the issue in your snippet.\nmini.ai checks vim.g.miniai_disable and vim.b.miniai_disable. Your autocmd is setting minianimate_disable, which belongs to a different module name and will not disable mini.ai.\nFor a buffer-local Visual-mode toggle, the variable needs to be miniai_disable and it needs to be true while you want mini.ai disabled, for example:\nvim.api.nvim_create_autocmd('ModeChanged', {\n  pattern = '*:[vV\\x16]*',\n  callback = function(args)\n    vim.b[args.buf].miniai_disable = true\n  end,\n})\n\nvim.api.nvim_create_autocmd('ModeChanged', {\n  pattern = '[vV\\x16]*:*',\n  callback = function(args)\n    vim.b[args.buf].miniai_disable = false\n  end,\n})\nThat disables the whole mini.ai module for that buffer while the flag is set. If you only want to free Neovim's built-in an/in while keeping some mini.ai textobjects, the cleaner path is to adjust the mini.ai mappings rather than toggling mini.ai by mode.",
